around|surrounding-position|PREPOSITION|Surrounding position or route|On different sides of something or along a route that goes round it.|xung quanh; vòng quanh|They planted herbs around the small fountain.|Họ trồng các loại rau thơm quanh đài phun nước nhỏ.|Around plus a noun phrase; round is also common, especially in British English.|0
around|in-the-vicinity|ADVERB|In the vicinity|In or near the place being discussed, without naming an exact position.|quanh đây; ở gần|Is there a repair shop around that can fix this zip?|Quanh đây có cửa hàng sửa chữa nào có thể sửa khóa kéo này không?|Can stand without a noun complement; look around means look in various directions.|1
harness|put-energy-to-use|VERB|Put power to useful work|To control a source of energy or an ability so that it can be used effectively.|khai thác; tận dụng|The rooftop equipment harnesses sunlight to heat water.|Thiết bị trên mái nhà tận dụng ánh nắng để làm nóng nước.|Transitive; harness energy, harness someone's skills. The direct object names the resource being used.|-
laundry|clothes-to-be-washed|NOUN|Clothes needing or receiving washing|Clothes and other washable fabric collected for washing, or the activity of washing them.|quần áo cần giặt; việc giặt giũ|We sorted the laundry by colour before starting the machine.|Chúng tôi phân loại quần áo cần giặt theo màu trước khi chạy máy.|Usually uncountable; do the laundry, a basket of laundry. Do not use a laundry to mean one garment.|-
outlaw|person-outside-the-law|NOUN|Person living outside the law|A person who breaks the law and evades its authorities, especially in historical stories.|kẻ ngoài vòng pháp luật|In the novel, an outlaw hides in the hills after escaping from prison.|Trong tiểu thuyết, một kẻ ngoài vòng pháp luật trốn trên đồi sau khi vượt ngục.|Countable; an outlaw, a band of outlaws. Often historical or associated with adventure stories.|-
shake|move-back-and-forth|VERB|Move back and forth|To move something repeatedly and quickly in different directions.|lắc|Shake the sealed jar gently to mix the two liquids.|Lắc nhẹ chiếc lọ đã đậy kín để trộn hai chất lỏng.|Transitive; shake, shook, shaken. Shake something gently or vigorously.|0
shake|tremble-or-vibrate|VERB|Tremble or vibrate|To make repeated small movements, often because of cold, emotion or a force.|run; rung|The windows shook as the heavy truck passed the house.|Các cửa sổ rung lên khi chiếc xe tải nặng chạy qua nhà.|Intransitive; shake with cold or fear. Past shook, past participle shaken.|2
shake|greeting-handshake|VERB|Shake hands in greeting|To hold someone's hand and move it briefly up and down as a greeting or sign of agreement.|bắt tay|The two gardeners shook hands after agreeing on the shared fence.|Hai người làm vườn bắt tay sau khi thống nhất về hàng rào chung.|Shake hands with someone or shake someone's hand; shook and shaken are irregular forms.|3
shake|brief-shaking-movement|NOUN|Brief shaking movement|An act of moving something quickly back and forth.|cái lắc; lần rung lắc|A gentle shake loosened the sand inside the shoe.|Một cái lắc nhẹ làm cát trong giày rơi ra.|Countable; give something a shake. A shake of the head often expresses disagreement.|1
